### KDP cover/spine sizing addendum

For the current **7×10 in, Standard Color paperback**, calculate the cover dynamically from the **final interior page count**. KDP specifies Standard Color spine width as `page_count × 0.002252 in`. ([Amazon Kindle Direct Publishing][1])

```text
spine_width = page_count * 0.002252 in
cover_width = 7 + spine_width + 7 + 0.25 in
            = 14.25 + spine_width
cover_height = 10 + 0.25 in
             = 10.25 in
```

The `0.25"` is the required `0.125"` cover bleed on each outside edge. Generate the cover only after determining the exact final interior page count, and use that value for both the spine width and overall PDF dimensions. Spine text must remain at least `0.0625"` from either spine edge. ([Amazon Kindle Direct Publishing][1])

[1]: https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/G201953020?utm_source=chatgpt.com "Create a Paperback Cover"

